{
 "_how": "ROW 42+ \u2014 THE HUMAN LABEL, AND IT IS A LABEL AND NOT A READING. Every rectangle here was drawn by LOOKING at the picture: each frame was downscaled 3x, ruled with a 128 px grid in its own image coordinates, and read by eye; the numbers were then multiplied back to full resolution, so an edge is good to about +/-10 px (well under the 0.35 m the evaluator pairs at, which is ~60 px at this store's scale). What is labelled is the INNER GLAZED APERTURE \u2014 the glass and its cames \u2014 and not the stone surround or the architrave, because the surround is what the detector is forbidden to answer with. A wall with no glazed opening carries \"none\": true and an empty list, and those walls are the corpus's other half: without them a detector that answered \"window\" everywhere would score perfectly. Covered: every promoted wall in backdrops/ (63 manor + 8 cyberpunk-2) and all 9 servants_hall/E candidates, which is the wall the audit memo names as a plain painted window the detector loses. The candidates are labelled on their own frames but carry the promoted wall's scale and corners, which is the same geometry the promotion measured them under. THIS FILE IS GROUND TRUTH AND NOT OUTPUT: nothing in the detector may be tuned by writing here, and window_calibration.json \u2014 which compares the PLAN to the reading \u2014 is a content metric and is not this.",
 "_labelled": "2026-08-29",
